{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Gather for Me seventy men</b> — corresponding to the seventy souls who descended to Egypt, and corresponding to the seventy nations, and corresponding to the seventy names that the Holy One, blessed be He, possesses. And these are they: El, Elohim, YHWH [Adonai], One, Master, Mighty, I Am, Strong, Truth, Slow to Anger, Last — for He does not hand His sovereignty to another, Faithfulness, Cluster of Henna, Blessed, Creator, Great, Exalted, Redeemer, Mighty, Distinguished, The Knowing One, Assembly, Remembering, Living, Devout, Gracious, Searching, Strong, Wise, Good, Pure of Eyes, Upright, Dweller in Secret, Glory, Hidden One, Awesome, Exalted, Eternal, Preserver of Kindness, Bearer of Iniquity, Bearer of Transgression, Bearer of Sin, Avenger, Watchful, Cleansing, Dweller of the East, Selah, Forgiving, Most High, Hind, Mighty, Redeeming, Visiting, Rock, Deer, Hosts, Holy One, Jealous, Near, Compassionate, Exalted, First — who did not receive His sovereignty from another, Abundant in Kindness, Guardian, Judge, Ruler, Prince, Dweller of Eternity, Perfect, Mighty. And seventy names of Israel, and these are they: Wife of Youth, Rams of Righteousness, Chiefs, Brothers, Beloved, Nation, Mother, Men, Ephraim, Mighty Ones, Nobles, Nut, Awesome One, Band, Sons, Sons of the Living El, Sons of Abraham, Sons of Isaac, Firstborn, Young Men, My Daughters, Pure, Ascending, Nation, Great, Locked Garden, Locked Fountain, Laden Vine, Married, Holy Seed, Wise Ones, Good Ones, Unique Ones, Precious Ones, Israel, Jeshurun, Jacob, Joseph, Jews, Children, Dear Ones, Bride, Shoot, Vineyard, Priests, Ministers, Kings, Sealed Spring, Inheritance, Noble Ones, Beautiful, Youth, Plant, Treasure, Exalted Ones, Humble Ones, Congregation, Hebrews, Servants, Peoples, Redeemed Ones, Scattered Ones, Flock, Holy Ones, Acquired Ones, Many, Tender, Tribes of YH, Perfect Ones — end. And seventy names for Jerusalem. Crowns on the heh of אספה to teach you that they shall be expert and scrupulous in the five books of Torah:" "<b>עמך</b> — in gematria: יהו דומין (they are equal):"], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The list of seventy divine names and seventy names of Israel is a well-known midrashic catalog. The bracketed [אדני] appears in the Hebrew source, likely inserted to supply the full form of the abbreviated ה׳. The phrase 'ע\"כ' (עד כאן, 'until here') marks the end of the received list before the tagin remark."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:22.034315849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}